    <h1>Kiavi Rates in 2026</h1>
    <p class="lede">Kiavi doesn't publish a fixed rate sheet — pricing is quoted per deal. These are the real-world ranges and, more usefully, the levers that decide where you land in them.</p>

    <h2>Current rate ranges</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Rate range (typical)</th><th>Structure</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Bridge / fix-and-flip</td><td>~7.75% – 12%</td><td>12–24 mo, interest-only, points at closing</td></tr>
        <tr><td>DSCR rental (30-year)</td><td>~6.4% – 9.5% (promos as low as 5.75% advertised)</td><td>30-yr fixed, ARM, and interest-only options</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <p class="fineprint">Ranges observed as of late 2026. Kiavi reprices with the market and runs periodic rate promotions; your quote is the only number that counts, and the soft quote doesn't affect your credit.</p>

    <h2>What actually moves your Kiavi rate</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Experience tier.</strong> The number of exits (flips sold or rentals refinanced) in the last 24 months is the single biggest lever. 5+ exits gets the floor pricing; 0 exits pays roughly 1–2 points more in rate.</li>
      <li><strong>Leverage.</strong> Asking for 95% LTC costs more than 80%. On DSCR loans, 80% LTV prices worse than 70%.</li>
      <li><strong>Credit score.</strong> 660 is the gate; 740+ improves pricing, especially on DSCR loans.</li>
      <li><strong>DSCR itself.</strong> Rentals whose rent comfortably covers the payment (DSCR ≥ 1.2) price better than break-even deals.</li>
      <li><strong>Points vs. rate.</strong> Both products let you trade origination points against rate in either direction. Short holds usually favor paying rate, not points.</li>
    </ul>

    {% include "partials/cta.njk" %}

    <h2>Are Kiavi's rates good?</h2>
    <p>For experienced investors, Kiavi sits at the low end of the hard-money market — typically beating Groundfloor, RCN, and Upright on comparable bridge deals (see the <a href="/kiavi-vs/">head-to-head comparisons</a>). For brand-new investors the gap narrows, and a local lender who knows your market can occasionally beat Kiavi's first-timer tier. The right move is always the same: Kiavi's quote takes minutes and costs nothing, so get it first, then shop it.</p>

